  "term": "borderline intelligence",
  "definition": "Borderline intelligence refers to intellectual functioning in the borderline IQ range, about 70 to 85. In the source packet, it is described as part of borderline intellectual functioning, a neurodevelopmental condition linked with difficulties in thinking and social functioning, often alongside academic and behavioral problems.",
